# November 17, 2026: Douglas County, Kansas (Lawrence, Baldwin City, Lecompton, Clinton Lake, Lone Star). A first close pass,
# drawn at random by tools/choose.py (region ks). Trail ruts, a battlefield, a drowned town's leftovers at Clinton Lake,
# a CCC camp's stone remnants, and the territorial-era buildings that still stand.
# Facts from the linked sources only: National Register forms read as text from NPGallery (tools/page.py), the Kansas
# Historical Society's register summaries and Constitution Hall visit page, Douglas County's park pages, Clio entries
# written by the University of Kansas public history program, HMdb marker texts, Wikipedia read with tools/wiki_raw.py,
# and local news (Lawrence Journal-World, Lawrence Times, KOFO). Pins were checked on Esri satellite and the LiDAR sheet.
